## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to scope CBAs for privacy-preserving on-device ML and quantify energy, storage, bandwidth, and compliance trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning
- Gradient compression
- Privacy/compliance overhead
- Cost modeling
- Rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeCBA(params){
  const {devices, energyPerDevice, uplink, cloud, retention} = params;
  const energy = devices * energyPerDevice;
  const total = energy + uplink + cloud + retention;
  const breakeven = total / Math.max(1, (params.revenuePerUser || 1));
  return {energy, total, breakeven};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle drift and model staleness in rollout?
- What metrics would you track to decide go/no-go, and how would you test them in a pilot?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a pragmatic CBA for on-device decision logic that changes user experience while preserving privacy and reducing server load. Tests modeling of energy, storage, and regulatory costs alongside rollout governance.

## Key Concepts

- On-device decisioning and privacy
- Compute and energy modeling
- Data minimization and consent logging
- Telemetry footprint and storage planning
- Rollout gates and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo cost model for CBA
function cba(params) {
  const energy = params.cpuW * params.hours;
  const storage = params.rulesKB * params.devices / 1024;
  const savings = params.backendCostPerUnit * params.throughputReduction;
  const compliance = params.complianceCost;
  return energy + storage - savings + compliance;
}
```

