## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses a candidate's ability to translate product goals into a financially grounded technical plan, balancing on-device ML costs, user privacy, and rollout risk.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML cost modeling (energy, memory, inference latency)
- Data transfer savings and network impact
- Privacy controls and regulatory compliance
- OTA update cadence and maintenance costs
- Rollout strategy, drift monitoring, and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-cost model for CBA calculations
function cba(params) {
  const energy = params.inferences * params.energyPerInference;
  const memory = params.modelSize + params.cacheSize;
  const dataSavings = params.uploadSize * params.reductionRate;
  return { energy, memory, dataSavings };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Explore data-locality, privacy, and practical CBA modeling for a lightweight client-side feature in a cloud data platform.

## Key Concepts

- Data locality and offline caching
- Cost modeling: storage, compute, network
- Privacy/compliance: anonymization, retention, audits
- Rollout strategy and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateCBA(params) {
  // simple cost model placeholder
  const { storagePerUserMB, months, users } = params;
  const storageCostPerMB = 0.02; // hypothetical
  const totalStorage = storagePerUserMB * users * months;
  return totalStorage * storageCostPerMB;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust the model for enterprise vs SMB customers?
- What monitoring would you set to validate the forecast post-launch?
